module gunbc.rung_drop.roadmap_sizing_authored_to_derived

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.rung_drop { RungDrop, Standing, TypedDeclaration, ReplacementStaged }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, OutsideTheLadder }

// WHAT FELL, STATED AS THE LOSS AND NOT AS THE EDIT. gunbc.roadmap_forecast keys its cycle-time
// calibration population on a node's sizing cell: an accepted node's PR open-to-merge interval is
// admitted as a sample for that cell, and a forecast for an unaccepted node is built by calibrating
// its own cell against those samples. Every one of those cells was HAND-AUTHORED on the roadmap
// node, and this change deleted the authored fields rather than leaving them standing beside the
// deriver that replaces them. Until the deriver returns a cell, every derivation lands on
// SizingNotDerivable, gunbc.roadmap_forecast derived_node_sizings drops every node, and the
// forecast's NodeUnsized refusal arm fires over the whole graph, so schedule_forecast produces no
// projection at all.
//
// WHY THIS IS A DROP AND NOT A REPAIR, even though what was lost was a guess. The forecast's
// refusal was previously discriminating: a node with no authored cell refused and a node with one
// projected, so the arm separated two populations. It now fires unconditionally, which is a
// permanently-red control -- it carries no information about any particular node, and a consumer
// reading "no forecast" can no longer tell "this node is unplanned" from "nothing can be forecast
// at all". That is a real loss of a real signal, and pricing it as free because its input was an
// estimate would be exactly the rung inflation section 4b(1) forbids.
//
// WHY THE TEMPORARY RUNG IS OFF THE LADDER. The class is not a guarantee that fell a step; the
// forecast is an operation that lost its only input. Nothing is mitigated because nothing is
// attempted: the fold refuses before it reaches any node. Placing it low on the ladder would imply
// a residual projection that does not exist.
//
// WHAT IS NOT DROPPED, so the population is not read wider than it is. No dispatch, launch, spawn,
// admission or presentation path refused on a size before this change and none does after it:
// gunbc.dispatch_selection threaded a NodeSizing through selection and no branch read it; that
// passenger is RETYPED, not deleted -- it is now the two-arm SizingProfileExpectation, still
// carried through the resolve functions and still recorded on the receipt and the refusal, so a
// later profile policy has a declared place to read a derived size and a declared absent arm to
// refuse on. What no branch can do, before or after, is refuse a dispatch because a size is
// missing. The spawn request omits its two size keys, which the dashboard's both-or-neither
// argument pair accepts; and the roadmap page drops a badge. The forecast is the only consumer whose OUTPUT changes.
//
// FIVE CONTROLS ARE IN THE POPULATION, WHICH IS UNUSUAL AND IS DELIBERATE. The last five
// population entries are witnesses, not production functions: each asserted a property of the live
// calibration population -- located, counted, per-cell gaps, nothing but calibration in the
// refusal, the three live cells calibrating to their exact observed intervals, and the authored
// size distribution across the active rows being deliberate rather than one value copied down the
// file -- and their subject is precisely what this drop loses. A control whose subject no longer
// exists cannot be kept green without weakening what it asserts, which is how a wall becomes a
// decoration. They are retired by name here rather than deleted quietly, and the trigger below is
// the condition under which they become writable again against a real population. What replaces
// them meanwhile is one control that IS authorable and does the load-bearing job:
// test.claim.roadmap_forecast_witness.witness_live_graph_refuses_every_node_as_unsized_while_the_deriver_is_a_stub
// hands derived_node_sizings a two-node fixture and refuses NodeUnsized over that identity join --
// it goes red the day the deriver answers a cell, which is either this drop retiring or a
// regression that would otherwise be silent. RECEIPT: on this tree, temporarily making
// gunbc.roadmap_sizing derive_task_sizing return SizingDerived for subject fixture-stub-unsized-a
// (the identity of fixture_node(id: "stub-unsized-a")) turns
// test.claim.roadmap_forecast_witness.witness_live_graph_refuses_every_node_as_unsized_while_the_deriver_is_a_stub
// FAIL under `gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/test/claim/roadmap/roadmap_forecast_witness_test.dag --function witness_live_graph_refuses_every_node_as_unsized_while_the_deriver_is_a_stub --claim-run`;
// the committed stub leaves that same invocation PASS. Re-derive by repeating the mutation, not by
// reading this sentence. The history
// join keeps its own live control for the same reason:
// test.claim.roadmap_forecast_witness.witness_cited_acceptance_pr_history_refuses_every_link_as_unsized
// asserts that EVERY cited acceptance/pull link refuses as HistoryNodeUnsized, so the loss is
// measured as total and loud rather than left as four observations quietly becoming zero.
//
// THE TRIGGER NAMES THE CAPABILITY AND NOT THE ARTIFACT. "gunbc.roadmap_sizing derive_task_sizing
// is replaced" would be satisfied by any function that returns a cell, including one that guesses,
// and the capability would stay dead while the row retired. What must exist is a derivation that
// READS A TASK AND ANSWERS FROM IT: given a SizingSubject's title, description and exit criterion
// it returns an intricacy and a volume, on the real acceptance path, with a discriminating control
// showing two materially different subjects receiving different cells -- and the forecast
// calibrating and projecting from those cells end to end. A stub that returns a constant satisfies
// none of that.

data roadmap_sizing_authored_to_derived: RungDrop = RungDrop {
  identity: "roadmap_sizing_authored_to_derived" as NonEmptyStr,

  subject: "gunbc.roadmap_forecast schedule_forecast",

  declared: "2026-09-10",

  standing: Standing,

  declaration: TypedDeclaration {
    previous: Mitigatable,
    temporary: OutsideTheLadder,
    reason: ReplacementStaged {
      replacement: "gunbc.roadmap_sizing derive_task_sizing, whose SizingNotDerivable arm is the honest stub standing where the authored intricacy/volume fields used to be",
    },
    population: [
    "gunbc.roadmap_forecast schedule_forecast",
    "gunbc.roadmap_forecast build_node_forecast",
    "gunbc.roadmap_forecast path_to_node",
    "gunbc.roadmap_forecast calibration_gaps",
    "gunbc.roadmap_forecast observation_for_link",
    "gunbc.roadmap_presentation sizing_fact",
    "gunbc.roadmap_spawner sizing_json_members",
    "test.claim.roadmap_forecast_witness.witness_live_graph_refuses_with_located_counted_calibration_gaps",
    "test.claim.roadmap_forecast_witness.witness_live_graph_gap_count_matches_refusal_rows",
    "test.claim.roadmap_forecast_witness.witness_live_graph_refusal_is_only_calibration",
    "test.claim.roadmap_forecast_witness.witness_live_calibration_keeps_small_sample_intervals",
    "test.claim.roadmap_authority.witness_active_sizes_are_intentional_and_nonuniform"
    ],
    restoration_trigger: "a sizing derivation that reads a task and answers from it: given a gunbc.roadmap_sizing SizingSubject -- title, description, exit criterion -- derive_task_sizing returns an Intricacy and a Volume on the real acceptance path, with an executed discriminating control in which two materially different subjects receive different cells, and gunbc.roadmap_forecast calibrates and projects from those derived cells end to end. Replacing the stub with any function that returns a cell does NOT satisfy this trigger; a constant answer leaves the capability dead."
  }
}
